{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to use the new "},{"code":"withSnapshotTesting","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tool for customizing how snapshots are generated and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"diffs displayed."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/MigratingTo1.17","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/migratingto1.17"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This library is under constant development, and we are always looking for ways to simplify the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library, and make it more powerful. This version of the library has deprecated some APIs,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"introduced a new APIs, and includes beta support for Swift’s new native testing library.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Customizing-snapshots","text":"Customizing snapshots"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Currently there are two global variables in the library for customizing snapshot testing:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/isRecording"},{"type":"text","text":" determines whether new snapshots are generated and saved to disk when the test"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"runs."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/diffTool"},{"type":"text","text":" determines the command line tool that is used to inspect the diff of two files on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"disk."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"These customization options have a few downsides currently.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"First, because they are globals they can easily bleed over from test to test in unexpected ways."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"And further, Swift’s new testing library runs parallel tests in the same process, which is in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stark contrast to XCTest, which runs parallel tests in separate processes. This means there are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"even more chances for these globals to bleed from one test to another."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"And second, these options aren’t as granular as some of our users wanted. When "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/isRecording"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is true snapshots are generated and written to disk, and when it is false snapshots are not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"generated, "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"unless","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" a file is not present on disk. The a snapshot "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"is","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" generated. Some of our"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"users wanted an option between these two extremes, where snapshots would not be generated if the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"file does not exist on disk."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"And the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/diffTool"},{"type":"text","text":" variable allows one to specify a command line tool to use for visualizing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"diffs of files, but only works when the command line tool accepts a very narrow set of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arguments,  _e.g.:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"sh","code":["ksdiff \/path\/to\/file1.png \/path\/to\/file2.png"]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Because of these reasons, the globals ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/isRecording","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/diffTool","type":"reference"},{"text":" are now deprecated, and we","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have introduced a new tool that greatly improves upon all of these problems. There is now a function","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"called ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/withSnapshotTesting(record:diffTool:snapshotNaming:referenceStorage:locale:timeZone:calendar:operation:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for customizing snapshots. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"allows you to customize how the ","type":"text"},{"code":"assertSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tool behaves for a well-defined scope.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Rather than overriding ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRecording","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"diffTool","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directly in your tests, you can wrap your test in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"withSnapshotTesting","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"row","numberOfColumns":2,"columns":[{"size":1,"content":[{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Before","","func testFeature() {","  isRecording = true ","  diffTool = \"ksdiff\"","  assertSnapshot(…)","}"]}]},{"size":1,"content":[{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ After","","func testFeature() {","  withSnapshotTesting(record: .all, diffTool: .ksdiff) {","    assertSnapshot(…)","  }","}"]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you want to override the options for an entire test class, you can override the ","type":"text"},{"code":"invokeTest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"method of ","type":"text"},{"code":"XCTestCase","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"row","numberOfColumns":2,"columns":[{"size":1,"content":[{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Before","","class FeatureTests: XCTestCase {","  override func invokeTest() {","    isRecording = true ","    diffTool = \"ksdiff\"","    defer { ","      isRecording = false","      diffTool = nil","    }","    super.invokeTest()","  }","}"]}]},{"size":1,"content":[{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ After","","class FeatureTests: XCTestCase {","  override func invokeTest() {","    withSnapshotTesting(record: .all, diffTool: .ksdiff) {","      super.invokeTest()","    }","  }","}"]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"And if you want to override these settings for ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"all"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" tests, then you can implement a base","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"XCTestCase","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" subclass and have your tests inherit from it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Further, the ","type":"text"},{"code":"diffTool","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"record","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" arguments have extra customization capabilities:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"diffTool"},{"type":"text","text":" is now a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/DiffTool-swift.struct","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"function","type":"text"}],"overridingTitle":"function"},{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(String, String) -> String"},{"type":"text","text":" that is handed the current snapshot file and the failed snapshot"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"file. It can return the command that one can run to display a diff. For example, to use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ImageMagick’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"compare"},{"type":"text","text":" command and open the result in Preview.app:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["extension SnapshotTestingConfiguration.DiffTool {","  static let compare = Self { ","    \"compare \\\"\\($0)\\\" \\\"\\($1)\\\" png: | open -f -a Preview.app\" ","  }","}"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"record"},{"type":"text","text":" is now a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/Record-swift.struct","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"type","type":"text"}],"overridingTitle":"type"},{"type":"text","text":" with 4"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"choices: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"all"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"missing"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"never"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"failed"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"all","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": All snapshots will be generated and saved to disk."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"missing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": only the snapshots that are missing from the disk will be generated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and saved."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"never","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": No snapshots will be generated, even if they are missing. This option is appropriate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when running tests on CI so that re-tries of tests do not surprisingly pass after snapshots are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unexpectedly generated."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"failed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": Snapshots only for failing tests will be generated. This can be useful for tests"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that use precision thresholds so that passing tests do not re-record snapshots that are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subtly different but still within the threshold."}]}]}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Beta-support-for-Swift-Testing","text":"Beta support for Swift Testing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This release of the library provides beta support for Swift’s native Testing library. Prior to this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"release, using ","type":"text"},{"code":"assertSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Test","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" would result in a passing test no matter what. That is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"because under the hood ","type":"text"},{"code":"assertSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" uses ","type":"text"},{"code":"XCTFail","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to trigger test failures, but that does not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cause test failures when using Swift Testing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In version 1.17 the ","type":"text"},{"code":"assertSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" helper will now intelligently figure out if tests are running","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in an XCTest context or a Swift Testing context, and will determine if it should invoke "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"XCTFail"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Issue.record"},{"type":"text","text":" to trigger a test failure."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For the most part you can write tests for Swift Testing exactly as you would for XCTest. However,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"there is one major difference. In order to override a snapshot’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"overridingTitle":"configuration","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"configuration","type":"text"}],"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration","type":"reference"},{"text":" for a particular test or an entire suite you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"must use what are known as “test traits”:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SnapshotTesting","","@Suite(.snapshots(record: .all, diffTool: .ksdiff))","struct FeatureTests {","  …","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"That will override the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"diffTool"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"record"},{"text":" options for the entire ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureTests"},{"text":" suite.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"These traits can also be used on individual ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Test"},{"text":"s too.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Migrating to 1.17","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"SnapshotTesting"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting"]]},"references":{"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/SnapshotTestingConfiguration":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/snapshottestingconfiguration","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The configuration for a snapshot test."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/SnapshotTestingConfiguration/Record-swift.struct":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The record mode of the snapshot test."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Record"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/Record-swift.struct","kind":"symbol","title":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration.Record","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/snapshottestingconfiguration\/record-swift.struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Record"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/withSnapshotTesting(record:diffTool:snapshotNaming:referenceStorage:locale:timeZone:calendar:operation:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"withSnapshotTesting"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"R"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"record"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Record","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV6RecordV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"diffTool"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DiffTool","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV8DiffToolV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"snapshotNaming"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnapshotNaming","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV0A6NamingO"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"referenceStorage"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ReferenceStorage","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV16ReferenceStorageO"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"locale"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Locale","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation6LocaleV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"timeZone"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TimeZone","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation8TimeZoneV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"calendar"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Calendar","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation8CalendarV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"operation"},{"kind":"text","text":": () "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"R"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"rethrows"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"R"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/withSnapshotTesting(record:diffTool:snapshotNaming:referenceStorage:locale:timeZone:calendar:operation:)","kind":"symbol","title":"withSnapshotTesting(record:diffTool:snapshotNaming:referenceStorage:locale:timeZone:calendar:operation:)","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/withsnapshottesting(record:difftool:snapshotnaming:referencestorage:locale:timezone:calendar:operation:)","abstract":[{"text":"Customizes ","type":"text"},{"code":"assertSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the duration of an operation.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/isRecording":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isRecording"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/isRecording","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/isrecording","kind":"symbol","title":"isRecording","deprecated":true,"abstract":[{"text":"Whether or not to record all new references.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/SnapshotTestingConfiguration/DiffTool-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DiffTool"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/DiffTool-swift.struct","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/snapshottestingconfiguration\/difftool-swift.struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DiffTool"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration.DiffTool","abstract":[{"text":"Describes the diff command used to diff two files on disk.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Powerfully flexible snapshot testing.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"SnapshotTesting"},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/diffTool":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"diffTool"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DiffTool","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV8DiffToolV"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/diffTool","deprecated":true,"url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/difftool","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Enhances failure messages with a command line diff tool expression that can be copied and pasted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into a terminal."}],"type":"topic","title":"diffTool"}}}